  "answer": "No, you cannot claim compensation for a delay caused by an air traffic control strike. Strikes are classified as extraordinary circumstances, which do not entitle you to compensation under Corvina Airways' policy. However, you are still entitled to the care provisions, such as meal vouchers and hotel accommodation if the delay requires an overnight stay. If the delay reached 5 hours or more, you may also choose to receive a full refund of your unused ticket and a return flight to your first point of departure, if applicable. Please note that claims must be submitted through the online form within 12 months of the flight date.",
